      "writtenOn": "2023-12-19T09:02:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately, I couldn\u0027t access Treehugger Presubmit Explainer (https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/kernel/common/+/2879768/1?tab\u003dchecks\u0026checksPatchset\u003d1\u0026checksRunsSelected\u003dTreehugger%20Presubmit%20Explainer)\nI think I have no permission for that.\nSo, I couldn\u0027t find why it makes fails exactly.\n\nI guess some your test targets enable CONFIG_SPIDEV\u003dm or some drivers call \"spi_slave_abort\". I thought the patch should be splited to gki_defconfig and adding spi_slave_abort to our symbol list\n\nif there is no KMI broken with this change and passes Treehugger Robot,\nis it okay to make a single patch which enables gki_defconfig and adds new symbol to symbol list?",
      "parentUuid": "ee5c7ddf_b976173f",
      "revId": "104ae39d0b4cebc387ce31e902288a1b4b7a4780",
